id: pm-gh1756
title: "GH-1756: pm context counts in_progress_unowned and in_progress_idle over a different population than in_progress"
description: "Reported in GH-1756 against 2026.11.18. With a custom progress status (workflow.in_progress_status set to doing), the summary's in_progress counts items by the status role, but in_progress_unowned and in_progress_idle count items by the configured progress status. When doing carries the blocked role, pm context reports in_progress 0 alongside in_progress_unowned 2 and in_progress_idle 2, so the advisories exceed their own total. All three counts must describe the same population. The unowned in-progress hygiene and the idle advisory that introduced these counts are related."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: advisories,"area:context","gh:1756",in-progress,status-roles
created_at: "2026-11-19T00:19:36.461Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-20T05:34:47.519Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-20T05:12:58.002Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-20T05:12:58.002Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "For any status-role configuration, in_progress_unowned and in_progress_idle never exceed in_progress; A custom progress status is counted consistently by all three summary fields; Tests cover a custom progress status with the blocked role and with the active role"
parent: pm-dj98
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "summary.in_progress counts every item in workflow.in_progress_status, the predicate the advisory scan and the focus ranking already use, while open stays the active items outside that status, so active_items equals open plus in_progress whenever the progress status carries the active role. ContextSummary, COMMANDS.md and MUTATION_INTEGRITY.md document the population; contract_change declares the non-default-workflow difference."
expected_result: "in_progress, in_progress_unowned and in_progress_idle count the same population, so neither advisory exceeds in_progress for any status-role configuration."
actual_result: "With a doing progress status carrying the blocked role, context reports in_progress 2, in_progress_unowned 2, in_progress_idle 2, active_items 1 and open 1; with the active role, 2/2/2 with active_items 3 and open 1. Counting over active items only (the old code) fails the spec with in_progress 0; the full suite passes."
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
