  pm-w8q4,related,"2026-11-19T00:19:36.461Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-20T05:34:32.926Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review of the first head raised two findings, both fixed. (1) The workflow may name the progress status by an alias: the advisory scan resolved it through the registry but the summary compared item statuses with the raw id, so an aliased status still gave in_progress 0 beside advisories 2/2. context.ts now resolves the progress status once (progressStatusOf) for the summary counts, the focus rank, the open/in-progress predicates and returned focus row states. (2) The markdown summary printed in_progress inside active_items even when the progress status is not active; it now renders on its own line marked outside active_items, and WORKSPACE_POSITION_AND_LIFECYCLE.md qualifies the active_items = open + in_progress guarantee. Specs cover the alias and both renderings."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  src/sdk/query/context.ts,project,summary in_progress counts the configured progress status like both advisories (GH-1756)
  tests/unit/commands/governance/health-in-progress-work.spec.ts,project,custom doing status with the blocked and the active role
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/commands/governance/health-in-progress-work.spec.ts tests/unit/commands/query/context-command.spec.ts,project,300,"harness:claude-code","2026-11-20T04:51:32.174Z",local_mutation,fix/diagnostic-population-truth
docs[3]{path,scope,note}:
  docs/COMMANDS.md,project,context in-progress population
  docs/MUTATION_INTEGRITY.md,project,context in-progress population
  docs/WORKSPACE_POSITION_AND_LIFECYCLE.md,project,active_items equation qualified for a non-active progress status
close_reason: pm context counts in_progress and both in-progress advisories over one population
contract_change:
  api: pm context summary.in_progress
  before: "summary.in_progress counted only items in the progress status that also carried the active role, compared by the raw workflow id, while in_progress_unowned and in_progress_idle counted every item in that status, so the advisories could exceed the total"
  after: "summary.in_progress counts every item in workflow.in_progress_status, alias-resolved and whatever role it carries, the same population as both advisories; open stays the active items outside it, and markdown renders a non-active progress count apart from active_items"
  migrate: "No change for the default workflow, where the progress status carries the active role. With a non-active progress status, read in_progress as the count of items in that status rather than active_items - open"
escape_class: production_defect
gate_evidence:
  disposition: gate_strengthened
  owner: pm-gh1756
  gate_id: test-coverage
  negative_control: "Counting summary.in_progress over active-role items only, as before, fails the GH-1756 spec in tests/unit/commands/governance/health-in-progress-work.spec.ts with in_progress 0 against advisories 2/2 for a progress status carrying the blocked role"
  local_checks[3]: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/commands/governance/health-in-progress-work.spec.ts tests/unit/commands/query/context-command.spec.ts,node scripts/run-tests.mjs test,pnpm typecheck
  hosted_checks[2]: CI / Gates (static),CI / Gates (coverage)
